# Field table: MoldUDP64 (Nasdaq, "MoldUDP64 Protocol Specification", V 1.00,
# last revision 8/2/24), the multicast transport of TotalView-ITCH 5.0.
# Offsets are 0-based from the start of the UDP payload. Every number field is a
# big-endian binary integer (spec p.2, Assumptions), including those the tables
# mark NUM.
#
# A downstream packet is this 20-byte header followed by MessageCount message
# blocks, each a 2-byte big-endian length that excludes itself followed by that
# many bytes of message data (p.4, Message Block). The message blocks are read
# with the ITCH decoder (itch50.tbl), whose @length_prefix is that length.
@venue nasdaq
@endian big
@pad space
@type ANUM char
@type NUM uint

### mold::from_nasdaq

MessageType - 0 0 # DownstreamPacketHeader: header of every multicast or retransmitted packet (MoldUDP64 V1.00, p.3, Downstream Packet / Header)
@size 20
Session ANUM 0 10 # Session the packet belongs to; padding not stated
SequenceNumber NUM 10 8 # Sequence number of the first message in the packet; later messages are numbered implicitly
MessageCount NUM 18 2 # Message blocks in the packet; 0 heartbeat, 0xFFFF end of session (p.3, p.4)

### mold::to_nasdaq

MessageType - 0 0 # RequestPacket: retransmission request sent by UDP unicast to a re-request server (p.5, Request Packet)
@size 20
Session ANUM 0 10 # Session the request belongs to
SequenceNumber NUM 10 8 # First requested sequence number
RequestedMessageCount NUM 18 2 # Messages requested; the reply holds only as many as fit in one UDP packet

### end
